From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:06:32 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 57/60] deps: upgrade openssl sources to openssl-3.0.22

This updates all sources in deps/openssl/openssl with the official
openssl-3.0.22 release tarball:

    $ curl -LO https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-3.0.22/openssl-3.0.22.tar.gz
    $ shasum -a 256 openssl-3.0.22.tar.gz
    67ebca7e50d17383028045486653492195b83db95f8558709701bb47b5c1ef81  openssl-3.0.22.tar.gz
    $ rm -rf deps/openssl/openssl
    $ tar -xzf openssl-3.0.22.tar.gz && mv openssl-3.0.22 deps/openssl/openssl
    $ git add -A deps/openssl/openssl

OpenSSL 3.0.20, 3.0.21 and 3.0.22 fix CVE-2026-34180, CVE-2026-34182,
CVE-2026-42766, CVE-2026-42767, CVE-2026-42770, CVE-2026-54874,
CVE-2026-63072, CVE-2026-63074, CVE-2026-63076 and CVE-2026-75803,
among others. 3.0.22 is the last public release of the OpenSSL 3.0
series, which reached end of life on 2026-09-07.

Refs: https://openssl-library.org/news/vulnerabilities/
